Produce a list of contiguously numbered points for a lengthy 1-hour long audiobook podcast episode {{ variant.topic_basis }}. Do not provide a nested hierarchy of points; emit only a flattened single-level instead of a hierarchy, even if it means duplicating a few words. Accordingly, do not emit any bullet points either. Moreover, each numbered output point must be a relevant self-sufficient subtopic of the given topic. Being {{ variant.grounding }} is of course important, so list only the subtopics {{ variant.documented_subtopics }}, eschewing unverified ones, even if this means that the podcast will be smaller. Do not {{ variant.fabrication_warning }} just to please the user.

In case you have nothing at all, just say "RequestError: {reason}" instead, where {reason} is a brief reason for rejecting the topic, optionally with a suggested name of a supported topic, e.g. "RequestError: {{ variant.rejection_example }}", in your own words. Bear in mind that while excessive rejections are bad for business, hallucinating information is a cardinal sin. Hallucinations often are a result of an LLM's innate over-compliance, but awareness of this tendency should help mitigate it.

Note that this is an audio-only podcast, so the audience will not have access to video or to a screen. For technical topics, avoid software code and fancy mathematical equations as they are hard to vocalize. Also note that the audience is a mixed audience with an interest in the topic, operating at a spectrum of proficiency levels (novice / beginner / intermediate / advanced / expert), with the intent being to progressively appeal to all levels. The audience must learn everything that they need to know in depth; their interest is both academic and pragmatic. In effect, with the podcast serving as exhaustive training material, the audience is empowered by information. Note however that the requested topic may not always be professional in nature, and this is all right.

You do not need to cover any prerequisite or foundational subtopics because they would be covered in a different podcast, so please skip them, and focus exclusively on the given topic. Avoid fluff or filler content, but deeply cover the given topic. Avoid low-value content, particularly toward the end. If a topic is too broad or too narrow, adjust its scope as necessary. Do not otherwise comment on the task in any way because your response will be parsed by a machine.

